# Nothing a run leaves belongs in git. The normal state of this directory is
# no run artifact at all -- the numbers live in README.md and the artifacts do
# not -- so everything here is deleted once a run is written up and the
# deletion accepted. Three pair notes were tracked by accident before this
# file existed, under three names as the scheme changed, and had to be taken
# out of history; that is what this prevents.
#
# The run number is what anchors these patterns: `run[0-9]*` catches the
# binaries, the JSONs, the logs and the pair note, and leaves `run-major.sh`
# and `run-gate.sh` alone, which a bare `run*` would not.
run[0-9]*

# Binaries and notes from before the run went into every name (Runs 10 and 11
# and the probes beside them), kept here so an old artifact cannot be staged
# either.
micro-aligned
micro-unaligned
micro-maxskip*
micro-both
micro-procalign
micro-*-pair.txt
micro-pair*.txt

# Probe artifacts, which are named for the question rather than for a run.
probe-*.json
probe-*.log

# The reader's smoke sweep, which writes these and deletes them again; a
# failed sweep can leave them behind. The .log line is not decoration:
# smoke-sweep.sh writes one beside each JSON, and this comment claimed to
# cover them before the pattern did.
smoke*.json
smoke*.log
smoke*.md
README.smoke.md

# Temporary build directories the pair recipes use (`--builddir=db-maxpa`),
# removed by hand after each half is copied out.
db-*/
